    <string name="faq_q1">Does the app need Internet?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Prayer times are computed on the device and adhkar are built in. Internet is only needed to listen to and download adhan voices (Islamweb) and to show the map.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">How do I change the adhan voice?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">More → App settings → Adhan voice: search, listen, then tap “Adopt” to download it.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Why does the app ask for exact alarms?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">To schedule the adhan like an alarm clock so it fires exactly on time, even in battery saver mode.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">The adhan doesn\'t fire on some phones?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Enable the battery exemption and autostart in settings, and allow notifications and lock-screen display.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">How do I change the calculation method or school?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">More → App settings → Calculation. The method is chosen automatically by country and can be changed.</string>
    <string name="faq_q6">What are iqama settings for?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">They set the delay between adhan and iqama; the home screen then shows a countdown to iqama after the adhan.</string>
    <string name="faq_q7">How does the Qibla compass work?</string>
    <string name="faq_a7">It uses the phone\'s orientation sensor and your city coordinates. Move the phone in a figure 8 to calibrate it.</string>

    <string name="privacy_t1">No data collection</string>
    <string name="privacy_b1">No personal data is collected. The only connections fetch adhan files (Islamweb) and map tiles (OpenStreetMap).</string>
    <string name="privacy_t2">Location</string>
    <string name="privacy_b2">If you choose automatic location, GPS is used once to find the nearest city; coordinates stay on your device.</string>
    <string name="privacy_t3">Storage</string>
    <string name="privacy_b3">Your settings (city, adhan, iqama, favorites) and the downloaded audio file are stored locally and removed when you uninstall.</string>
    <string name="privacy_t4">Permissions</string>
    <string name="privacy_b4">Exact alarms, notifications and lock-screen display are used solely to play the adhan on time.</string>
    <string name="privacy_t5">Sources</string>
    <string name="privacy_b5">Adhan voices: audio.islamweb.net; times: the open-source adhan library; map: OpenStreetMap.</string>
